---
title: State diagram - user account (User.IsActive, User.EmailConfirmed)
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR

    state "Registered, unconfirmed<br>IsActive = true<br>EmailConfirmed = false<br>(cannot sign in)" as Unconfirmed
    state "Active<br>IsActive = true<br>EmailConfirmed = true<br>(can sign in)" as Active
    state "Inactive<br>IsActive = false<br>(cannot sign in or refresh)" as Inactive

    [*] --> Unconfirmed : register
    [*] --> Active : seeded
    Unconfirmed --> Active : confirm (NOT IMPLEMENTED)
    Active --> Inactive : suspend
    Active --> Inactive : soft delete
    Inactive --> Active : reinstate
    Active --> Active : reset password

    note right of Inactive
        register = POST /api/auth/register (role Client)
        suspend = PATCH /api/admin/users/{id}/suspend, audit "Suspended user"
        soft delete = DELETE /api/admin/users/{id}, audit "Deactivated user"
        reinstate = PATCH /api/admin/users/{id}/reinstate, audit "Reinstated user"
        reset password = POST /api/auth/reset-password (new hash, refresh tokens revoked)

        Suspended and soft-deleted are the SAME stored state (IsActive = false),
        so reinstate also undoes a delete. Repeating suspend, delete or
        reinstate returns 409.
        No lockout state: no failed-attempt counter, only the per-IP
        rate limit (5 sign-in requests per minute, 429).
    end note
